<h2>Who has the problem</h2>
<p><b>Pays and decides:</b> the registered manager or service owner. <b>Who uses it?</b> Home support workers direct to their phone.</p>
<p class="box">“I get the same phone calls daily, asking repetitive questions, and the answer is already stated in the policy.” <i>(invented quote)</i></p>
<h2>What the solution must do</h2>
<table><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>How it is met</th><th>Status</th></tr>
<tr><td>Decision in 3 taps or fewer</td><td>Tap a request; the answer appears</td><td><span class="tg ok">In the demo</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Shows the rule it came from</td><td>Rule, policy area and review date on every result</td><td><span class="tg ok">In the demo</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Works on a phone</td><td>Large buttons, one column, no login</td><td><span class="tg ok">In the demo</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Unclear or risky requests go to a manager</td><td>Medication, money, no rule, or an out-of-date rule</td><td><span class="tg ok">In the demo</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Manager sees escalations</td><td>Count and list at the bottom of the demo</td><td><span class="tg ok">In the demo</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Understands free-text requests</td><td>An AI language model would read typed requests</td><td><span class="tg pl">Planned</span></td></tr></table>
<p>The demo is a rule-based engine, not an AI model. An AI version is planned. The 50 policy records are invented sample data. If a rule was last reviewed over 365 days ago, the demo flags it and sends permitted tasks to a manager.</p>

